<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh March oil output rises to 2.14 mln T.</title>
<headline>Kazakh March oil output rises to 2.14 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan's production of crude oil and gas condensate rose in March to 2.14 million tonnes from 1.90 million tonnes in February, the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The committee released the following figures for energy output in its latest monthly statistical bulletin. Figures in tonnes, except crude oil in million tonnes and natural gas in billion cubic meters).</p>
<p> KAZAKH ENERGY OUTPUT	March 97     Feb 97     Jan-March 97</p>
<p> Crude oil		     2.138	  1.897	 6.149</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	+12.7	  -10.2	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	+12.2	  +12.2	 +14.2</p>
<p> Natural gas		   0.67	   0.61	  1.97</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	+10.5	  -10.1	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	+17.0	  +19.1	 +18.1</p>
<p> Gasoline		    116,900	122,700     346,200</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct chang	 -4.7	  +15.1	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct chane	-40.0	  -37.0	 -40.7</p>
<p> Diesel			207,900	185,400     589,200</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct chnge	+12.1	   -5.4	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change     -26.6	   +3.3	 -15.9</p>
<p> Fuel oil		    294,100	285,700     924,000</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	+2.9	  -17.0	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change     -13.4	  -20.4	  -9.5</p>
<p>-- Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
